## Design Philosophy

Traditional PRDs were written for human developers in sprint planning meetings.
They assumed shared context, verbal clarification, and iterative back-and-forth.

AI-assisted development changes that contract. Agents and AI-enabled teams work
best with:

- **Explicit requirements** — nothing assumed, nothing verbal
- **Traceable structure** — every requirement linked to a test case
- **Clear constraints** — hard boundaries stated upfront, not discovered mid-build
- **Unambiguous success conditions** — the agent knows exactly when it is done

These templates are built around those principles. They are also intentionally
useful for traditional teams — the discipline that makes a good AI handoff
makes a good human handoff too.

